# English screen corpus for iomoont (the PRESS START tournament MOD), at the
# Netherlands country default (SW40-2/3/4 = country 4, English text, F11).
# No DIP override is set: the DEFAULT in SLEIC2_COMPORTS already selects it.
#
# Boot, a full attract cycle, coin + credit, a three-ball game exercising
# every playfield feature (both ramps, the orbit lane, all five bumpers
# twice round, both bull eyes, the drop bank walked to 2/4/5 targets, the
# inner bank, both holes, Jupiter's lock twice for multiball, two tilt
# warnings to a full tilt -- tilt warns defaults to 1, F10), the mod's own
# PRESS START screen at the normal end-of-game hook (D5123), one START to
# clear it, and whatever the post-game sequence shows next (high-score entry
# if the score qualifies, otherwise straight back to attract), then the
# whole 38-record service-menu tree (SOUND/VIDEO, GAME, TECHNICAL -- F14).
#
# Keys: L/R Ctrl + R/H/B qualify Ramp, Hole, Bull Eye 1 vs 2; W/E/D/F/G are
# Bumpers 1-5; J Jupiter; I Inner Bank; O Lane 10 (orbit); K Lane 11;
# Z/X/C/V/N Drop targets A-E; Y/U/A/S/M/L/,/./ Lanes 1-9; Q Drain; Space
# plunges; Down follows the next ball after a drain (src/wpc/sims/sleic/
# iomoon.c).  1/5/7/T are START/COIN/TEST/TILT (sleic.h SLEIC_CABPORT); in
# the service menu, the left/right flipper keys (LShift/RShift) scroll and
# select, START backs up one level, and TEST opens or fully closes the menu
# regardless of depth (confirmed empirically, not stated in F14 as such).
#
# Two things earned from running this against the real binary, not guessed:
#
# - A key script mark must be placed AT OR BEFORE the action that changes
#   the screen, never after it with the action still to come -- a mark's
#   scene runs to the NEXT mark, so any action scheduled before that next
#   mark (even one meant for a "later" step) is what the scene's last frame
#   -- its repr -- actually shows.  Every entry below marks a record, then
#   sends the key that enters it, on the same frame.
# - The three auto-cycling TECNICO tests (SOLENOIDS, the three LIGHT TESTs)
#   render their own "LIGHT: LCn" text reliably only right after boot or one
#   bare reboot; once several other menu records have been visited first,
#   the same test still runs (confirmed: the parent list still redraws
#   correctly on exit) but stops showing decodable text for the rest of the
#   session. Not explained; the walk below visits these first for that
#   reason, and the report says which ones this actually caught text on.
#
# - Pressing extra keys (a walked high-score wheel, an extra START) after
#   the PRESS START gate, on top of the single press that actually clears
#   it, left the machine not answering a fresh TEST press for a long time
#   afterward (tried up to a 22000-frame wait -- still nothing); a single
#   clean START and nothing else does not have this problem, which is why
#   the script below sends only that one press. Not narrowed down further.
#
# A second coin + START cycle, tried separately to roll for the mod's
# SPECIAL trampoline (D5077, the match-win path) by chaining several quick
# games, ran into the same kind of post-game unresponsiveness before it was
# diagnosed and is not included here; only the normal end-of-game hook
# (D5123) is deliberately exercised. See the task report for what was tried.
    40 mark boot
    40 tap 8 KEYCODE_1
   640 mark attract
  1240 mark credit
  1240 tap 8 KEYCODE_5
  1360 mark ball-1-start
  1360 tap 8 KEYCODE_1
  1510 mark ball-1-in-play
  1510 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
  1630 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_R
  1700 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_R
  1770 tap 10 KEYCODE_O
  1840 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
  1910 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
  1980 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  2050 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  2120 tap 10 KEYCODE_W
  2190 tap 10 KEYCODE_E
  2260 tap 10 KEYCODE_D
  2330 tap 10 KEYCODE_F
